WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.720 --> 00:00:04.720
10.

00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:05.720
9.

00:00:05.720 --> 00:00:06.220
8.

00:00:06.220 --> 00:00:06.720
7.

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:12.360
(TOGETHER) 6, 5, 4, 3, 2, 1.

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:16.920
Ghostwriter, Beyond the Page.

00:00:16.920 --> 00:00:17.430
Hi!

00:00:17.430 --> 00:00:18.660
You're right on time.

00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:20.760
Welcome to Ghostwriter, Beyond the Page.

00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:23.790
I'm DJ MacHale, your host.

00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:26.460
I'm an author, a filmmaker, a book lover,

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:28.770
and I wrote one of the books from Ghostwriter.

00:00:28.770 --> 00:00:30.630
So I'm really excited about diving back

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:31.768
into the Ghostwriter world.

00:00:31.768 --> 00:00:33.810
And I'm really happy that you're joining me today

00:00:33.810 --> 00:00:34.800
on this journey.

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:38.070
Today we are going down the rabbit hole

00:00:38.070 --> 00:00:40.070
into Alice's Adventures in Wonderland.

00:00:40.070 --> 00:00:41.820
And along the way, we're going to find out

00:00:41.820 --> 00:00:43.090
what Donna has been up to.

00:00:43.090 --> 00:00:45.715
Now, I understand she's getting very creative with her writing,

00:00:45.715 --> 00:00:47.850
and even started her own personal video diary.

00:00:47.850 --> 00:00:49.710
It sounds pretty cool.

00:00:49.710 --> 00:00:51.180
I think she's going to be wanting

00:00:51.180 --> 00:00:53.760
to write an original story of her own,

00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:56.370
but it sounds like she may be having a little bit of trouble

00:00:56.370 --> 00:00:57.970
getting started.

00:00:57.970 --> 00:00:59.640
So let's go see how she's doing.

00:00:59.640 --> 00:01:02.160
And hopefully, maybe, a special friend

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:06.170
will come along to give her a hand.

00:01:06.170 --> 00:01:09.230
Welcome to Donna's Video Diary.

00:01:09.230 --> 00:01:11.330
So here's the latest.

00:01:11.330 --> 00:01:14.660
Ever since Ghostwriter started releasing book characters,

00:01:14.660 --> 00:01:18.200
I've been thinking of writing something myself, a totally

00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:20.270
original story by yours truly.

00:01:20.270 --> 00:01:27.760
But so far, I've got nothing.

00:01:27.760 --> 00:01:30.700
I just can't figure out the best way to start.

00:01:30.700 --> 00:01:32.750
This is kind of new territory for me,

00:01:32.750 --> 00:01:35.890
so I'm a little nervous.

00:01:35.890 --> 00:01:38.110
Curtis is at dad's house, and I'm spending some time

00:01:38.110 --> 00:01:39.280
at mom's house.

00:01:39.280 --> 00:01:42.700
I definitely don't hate having my own room,

00:01:42.700 --> 00:01:44.860
but I do kind of wish there was someone I could

00:01:44.860 --> 00:01:48.120
bounce some ideas around with.

00:01:48.120 --> 00:01:51.120
Maybe Ghostwriter could help me bring my story to life.

00:01:54.410 --> 00:01:57.290
Actually, that's not a bad idea.

00:01:57.290 --> 00:01:59.135
GW really does understand stories.

00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:07.650
Hey, Ghostwriter, if you're around and maybe bored,

00:02:07.650 --> 00:02:11.222
I would love it if you could help me write my story.

00:02:11.222 --> 00:02:11.930
Just let me know.

00:02:16.570 --> 00:02:18.280
Well, it was a long shot anyway.

00:02:23.780 --> 00:02:25.370
What?

00:02:25.370 --> 00:02:28.260
Or, I mean, who?

00:02:28.260 --> 00:02:31.400
It looks like Ghostwriter does want to help out after all.

00:02:31.400 --> 00:02:32.390
OK.

00:02:32.390 --> 00:02:33.480
Let me think.

00:02:33.480 --> 00:02:33.980
Who?

00:02:37.764 --> 00:02:38.264
Who?

00:02:42.550 --> 00:02:47.200
Maybe this isn't such a helpful hint after all.

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:49.580
Who?

00:02:49.580 --> 00:02:50.080
Who?

00:02:52.960 --> 00:02:54.102
Who?

00:02:54.102 --> 00:02:55.730
Who what?

00:02:55.730 --> 00:02:56.960
Alice?

00:02:56.960 --> 00:02:58.880
Where did you come from?

00:02:58.880 --> 00:02:59.990
It's so good to see you.

00:02:59.990 --> 00:03:03.260
Oh, it's so good to see you, too, Donna.

00:03:03.260 --> 00:03:05.400
So you were asking something.

00:03:05.400 --> 00:03:07.250
Ghostwriter must have sent her here to help.

00:03:10.460 --> 00:03:11.950
Actually, yes.

00:03:11.950 --> 00:03:14.390
But first, what are you doing?

00:03:14.390 --> 00:03:16.570
Oh, well, I was trying to figure out

00:03:16.570 --> 00:03:19.760
how to bring a little bit of Wonderland here to my sister.

00:03:19.760 --> 00:03:22.090
You know, I was really, really struggling

00:03:22.090 --> 00:03:23.470
when I was lost there.

00:03:23.470 --> 00:03:25.630
And apparently, I'm still struggling

00:03:25.630 --> 00:03:26.983
with this whole croquet thing.

00:03:26.983 --> 00:03:29.650
Though, it is much easier with a mallet and ball than a flamingo

00:03:29.650 --> 00:03:31.520
and hedgehog.

00:03:31.520 --> 00:03:34.420
Anyway, after my whole experience,

00:03:34.420 --> 00:03:39.798
I realized I learned a lot about who I am, and who I can be.

00:03:39.798 --> 00:03:42.340
So I wanted to share a taste of that adventure with my sister

00:03:42.340 --> 00:03:43.930
by throwing her a surprise tea party

00:03:43.930 --> 00:03:47.430
and croquet match with lots of cakes and tarts to eat.

00:03:47.430 --> 00:03:50.980
Oh, I really did love all the sweets in Wonderland.

00:03:50.980 --> 00:03:53.890
So it sounds like it's important to you

00:03:53.890 --> 00:03:57.160
to share what you liked and didn't like,

00:03:57.160 --> 00:04:01.450
and what you've been through, what makes you who you are,

00:04:01.450 --> 00:04:04.510
so basically your character.

00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:06.437
Yes, I guess you're right.

00:04:06.437 --> 00:04:08.020
In fact, that's one of the reasons why

00:04:08.020 --> 00:04:10.430
I want to write my own story and turn it into a book

00:04:10.430 --> 00:04:13.650
so I can share my experiences, which, I guess,

00:04:13.650 --> 00:04:16.930
would kind of make me the main character in it.

00:04:16.930 --> 00:04:19.180
Well, anyway, I really do have to go,

00:04:19.180 --> 00:04:21.910
but it was so lovely to talk to you again, Donna.

00:04:21.910 --> 00:04:23.150
Thanks, Alice.

00:04:23.150 --> 00:04:23.650
Good luck.

00:04:26.460 --> 00:04:28.830
Alice definitely figured out a lot about herself

00:04:28.830 --> 00:04:30.360
in Wonderland--

00:04:30.360 --> 00:04:34.320
enough to write a book about it with her as the hero.

00:04:34.320 --> 00:04:38.610
And if knowing who she is is so important to her story,

00:04:38.610 --> 00:04:41.250
maybe Ghostwriter is trying to tell me to first come up

00:04:41.250 --> 00:04:44.910
with my own main character.

00:04:44.910 --> 00:04:48.220
Alice is definitely the who of her story.

00:04:48.220 --> 00:04:50.130
So maybe reading more about her again

00:04:50.130 --> 00:04:52.510
will help me decide who the who of my story should be.

00:04:56.530 --> 00:04:58.990
The tunnel went straight for a long time,

00:04:58.990 --> 00:05:02.050
and Alice could hear the rabbit in the distance saying,

00:05:02.050 --> 00:05:05.170
"Oh, my ears and whiskers!" and "I'm so late!"

00:05:05.170 --> 00:05:09.070
Alice ran faster, so fast that it took her by surprise when

00:05:09.070 --> 00:05:11.440
the tunnel floor suddenly dropped away

00:05:11.440 --> 00:05:13.180
and she dropped with it--

00:05:13.180 --> 00:05:15.610
WHOOSH-- straight down.

00:05:15.610 --> 00:05:17.920
Falling is usually kind of scary,

00:05:17.920 --> 00:05:21.730
but this was a very long, slow, flowy fall.

00:05:21.730 --> 00:05:24.010
Alice was actually quite comfortable.

00:05:24.010 --> 00:05:27.130
Finally, she hit the bottom with a solid thump

00:05:27.130 --> 00:05:29.200
that didn't hurt a bit.

00:05:29.200 --> 00:05:32.230
Jumping up, Alice caught a glimpse of the rabbit's tail

00:05:32.230 --> 00:05:34.010
as it turned the corner.

00:05:34.010 --> 00:05:36.100
She hurried after it into a hallway,

00:05:36.100 --> 00:05:38.880
but when she got there, it was gone.

00:05:38.880 --> 00:05:41.230
As she tried to figure out what to do next,

00:05:41.230 --> 00:05:44.050
Alice saw that she was in a room with many doors

00:05:44.050 --> 00:05:46.510
of all different sizes and colors.

00:05:46.510 --> 00:05:49.360
She tried to open them, but they were all locked.

00:05:49.360 --> 00:05:51.700
"So annoying," she muttered to herself

00:05:51.700 --> 00:05:54.280
since there was no one else to mutter to.

00:05:54.280 --> 00:05:56.680
She added some extra-hard foot stomping

00:05:56.680 --> 00:05:58.138
just because she could.

00:05:58.138 --> 00:05:59.680
That was the kind of thing her sister

00:05:59.680 --> 00:06:01.210
would have complained about.

00:06:01.210 --> 00:06:03.250
But Serena wasn't there, so Alice

00:06:03.250 --> 00:06:07.270
felt free to stomp as hard and loud as she wanted to.

00:06:07.270 --> 00:06:09.550
It wasn't as much fun as she thought it would be,

00:06:09.550 --> 00:06:11.350
and a tingle at the back of her neck

00:06:11.350 --> 00:06:13.930
made her stop and turn around.

00:06:13.930 --> 00:06:15.640
A pretty little glass table stood

00:06:15.640 --> 00:06:19.360
in the middle of the room, and a gleaming gold key sat on top.

00:06:22.900 --> 00:06:26.290
Alice snatched it up and tried it in each locked door

00:06:26.290 --> 00:06:28.090
until she got to the smallest one--

00:06:28.090 --> 00:06:28.990
and the key fit.

00:06:31.540 --> 00:06:33.470
Alice opened the door.

00:06:33.470 --> 00:06:37.330
She was too big to fit through, so she bent down to take a peek

00:06:37.330 --> 00:06:40.510
and saw the most gorgeous garden she'd ever seen--

00:06:40.510 --> 00:06:44.860
rolling hills, sunflowers, and waterfalls.

00:06:44.860 --> 00:06:46.780
If only she could get herself small enough

00:06:46.780 --> 00:06:48.580
to fit through that tiny door!

00:06:48.580 --> 00:06:51.880
"There's got to be a way," said Alice, shutting the door.

00:06:51.880 --> 00:06:55.540
Because after chasing a talking, vest-wearing, watch-holding

00:06:55.540 --> 00:06:59.230
rabbit down a hole and finding a gold key,

00:06:59.230 --> 00:07:02.440
Alice figured there's always a way to do just about anything.

00:07:05.590 --> 00:07:07.510
Oh, hi.

00:07:07.510 --> 00:07:08.630
Nice to see you again.

00:07:15.810 --> 00:07:20.130
Well, I definitely learned a lot about Alice in that chapter.

00:07:20.130 --> 00:07:24.610
She clearly likes foot-stomping and beautiful gardens.

00:07:24.610 --> 00:07:28.030
She's also really determined and resilient.

00:07:28.030 --> 00:07:29.950
It seems like she'll stop at nothing to find

00:07:29.950 --> 00:07:31.510
a way through that door.

00:07:31.510 --> 00:07:33.100
Talk about persistence.

00:07:33.100 --> 00:07:35.590
If I'm right and Ghostwriter is trying

00:07:35.590 --> 00:07:38.170
to help me create my main character,

00:07:38.170 --> 00:07:41.400
I'll need to start with who and what they are.

00:07:41.400 --> 00:07:46.120
I'll have to find description words, likes, dislikes,

00:07:46.120 --> 00:07:49.840
strengths, weaknesses, and even relationships,

00:07:49.840 --> 00:07:52.900
like Alice and her sister.

00:07:52.900 --> 00:07:53.840
OK.

00:07:53.840 --> 00:07:57.980
I've got a lot to think about, but I know one thing for sure.

00:07:57.980 --> 00:08:00.065
My character will be super into fashion.

00:08:02.720 --> 00:08:05.553
I'm starting to feel really good about this.

00:08:05.553 --> 00:08:06.470
Time to start writing.

00:08:12.290 --> 00:08:14.630
It looks like Donna is finally off to a good start

00:08:14.630 --> 00:08:18.060
thanks to all the help she got from Ghostwriter.

00:08:18.060 --> 00:08:20.115
Now, when you're writing a story,

00:08:20.115 --> 00:08:22.490
it's really important to come up with an interesting main

00:08:22.490 --> 00:08:25.730
character, because that's who your story is about, right?

00:08:25.730 --> 00:08:27.098
And who is that character?

00:08:27.098 --> 00:08:27.890
What are they like?

00:08:27.890 --> 00:08:29.160
It's up to you.

00:08:29.160 --> 00:08:31.730
And when you're working on it, it's

00:08:31.730 --> 00:08:34.460
a good idea to get those ideas down in a journal.

00:08:34.460 --> 00:08:36.919
And it doesn't have to be a fancy pantsy journal like this.

00:08:36.919 --> 00:08:39.110
It could just be a couple of sheets of paper.

00:08:39.110 --> 00:08:40.289
That's all you need.

00:08:40.289 --> 00:08:43.280
And if you want to dive deeper into the Ghostwriter world,

00:08:43.280 --> 00:08:47.750
be sure to read Alice's Adventures in Wonderland,

00:08:47.750 --> 00:08:50.420
and then be sure to check out the Ghost in Wonderland section

00:08:50.420 --> 00:08:52.370
of the activity guide.

00:08:52.370 --> 00:08:55.550
And of course, join the rest of the Ghostwriter gang on Apple

00:08:55.550 --> 00:08:58.090
TV+ for more episodes of the show.

00:08:58.090 --> 00:08:59.830
Bye bye.

